<title>NORWAY: One-hour strike by Statoil supply workers planned.</title>
<headline>One-hour strike by Statoil supply workers planned.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Workers at Den Norske Stats Oljeselskap ASA's (Statoil) platform supply centre near Bergen planned a one-hour strike on Monday, but the walkout would not disrupt oil production, oil worker's union OFS said.</p>
<p>OFS manager Oddleiv Toennessen said the stoppage would take place between noon and 1 p.m. (1000-1100 GMT) at the Coast Centre Base (CCB). It was meant as a political protest against plans by Statoil to sell the unit to the British company Consolidated Supply Management Ltd.</p>
<p>&quot;This action will not affect oil production or prices,&quot; Toennessen said. &quot;The base supplies oil platforms with food and all kinds of equipment.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
